e it your only goal  to improve on one thing with each video  and i assure you that as time progresses  and you continue to post you will  improve now let's talk about a biggie  equipment and setup this is where i  think i did some things right but  mainly i just made a lot of mistakes  first off let me tell you what i started  off with i had this sony camera that i  had purchased several years back i had a  laptop a tripod and a smartphone but  when it came to lighting i definitely  needed something to lighten up the home  and so what i did is i walked over to  the tool shed and i confiscated some of  my husband's work lights and this is  actually what i'm currently using and i  have been using ever since i started the  youtube channel so i considered this a  smart move using what i already had but  because i knew that i had a disadvantage  by not having other social media  websites i began to binge watch tons and  tons of videos on how to start a youtube  channel how to set up a background and  all those sorts of things and i began to  feel very inadequate when i saw other  youtubers gear and setup and the awesome  quality of their images and i began to  feel like i needed that to be able to  grow and so i ended up purchasing a very  expensive and large gimbal the zion  weeble lab and i mean this thing is  super awesome it's really very cool you  can't tell me this is not one sexy piece  of equipment it can produce some awesome  images  but  there's a big butt  i didn't consider my lifestyle when i  purchased it this one was a mistake for  me because for someone who works  full-time as a mom of two and trying to  start a youtube channel i don't have the  flexibility to take my camera from  tripod to put it on the gimbal and  balancing it and carrying this big thing  around while i'm chasing after my kids  it just does not work for me and so  sadly when i do use it  it's a tripod  a very expensive and fancy tripod if i  could go back i would have just started  with